Z||000002||fyerstarter||04-15-2001||11:29 PM||||The really quick way to do it is to make a selection of the area you want to change. Either by using the color wand, the lasso, or the select by color range option, then adjust the hue/saturation.<P>[This message has been edited by fyerstarter (edited 04-15-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by fyerstarter (edited 04-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||04-16-2001||08:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fyerstarter:<BR>[B]Either by using the color wand, the lasso, or the select by color range option, then adjust the hue/saturation.<BR>B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats the simplest method there is. Can't get the desired shade the first time? Try to get close then just go straight back into hue saturation and adjust again from the new shade. Should take about 5 minutes or so at most.<P><BR>||||reg||1
